          "guid": "mt5hvflxtne2k9pm",
          "message": {
            "text": "TreeScope is part of Blink's SVG resource identity, so raw author ids cannot safely key a capture-wide map. The consumer and definition carry the same deterministic scope, and a ShadowRoot miss intentionally does not fall through to ownerDocument; renderer lookup and caches use the same pair. Pinned Chromium resolves mask/clip resources through OriginatingTreeScope SVGTreeScopedResources before geometry or Skia paint.",
            "markdown": "TreeScope is part of Blink's SVG resource identity, so raw author ids cannot safely key a capture-wide map. The consumer and definition carry the same deterministic scope, and a ShadowRoot miss intentionally does not fall through to ownerDocument; renderer lookup and caches use the same pair. Pinned Chromium resolves mask/clip resources through OriginatingTreeScope SVGTreeScopedResources before geometry or Skia paint."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/capture/script/walker/masks-clips.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 51,
                  "endLine": 60,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  // DOM ids are TreeScope-local. In particular, an outer document and a\n  // recursed same-origin iframe can both define `#m` without sharing an SVG\n  // resource. Keep the author id for diagnostics/serialization, but key the\n  // capture maps by the same deterministic scope carried by each consumer.\n  const scopedKey = (scope, id) => String(scope) + '\\u0000' + id;\n  const fragmentTarget = (el, id) => {\n    const root = el.getRootNode ? el.getRootNode() : el.ownerDocument;\n    if (root != null && typeof root.getElementById === 'function') {\n      return root.getElementById(id);\n    }"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
